{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>All</b> — The meaning of the psalm is clear, for all the evils that befell him were on account of bearing the reproach of the enemy." "<b>And the word מהוללי</b> — [it is] פָּעוֹלִים, who were in his eyes מהוללים; this is the one who makes himself מִתְהוֹלֵל by [swearing] by Elohim and by an oath: \"if I lie, let me be doubly [punished].\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {1 "The final phrase אם אכזב אהיה כפלני is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. It appears to illustrate the פָּעוֹלִים pattern: one who habitually swears falsely by Elohim, doubling his guilt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:48.815239885Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}